[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3806670249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3806670249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3806670249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i5S2p","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T18:02:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T18:02:05Z","body":"We discussed this PR briefly in the audio meeting. Makes sense to avoid copying into a buffer for no reason.\r\n\r\nAm I understanding it right that this is a performance optimization (reduced CPU load + RAM use)? If so, please provide benchmarks / profiles, as per our [optimization guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/optimization.html).\r\n\r\nW were also wondering if there could have been any reason for `get_file_as_bytes` to be used (caching perhaps?). Did you check if that may be the case?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3806670249/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3806946167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3806946167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3806946167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i6WN3","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T18:57:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T19:52:08Z","body":"> Am I understanding it right that this is a performance optimization (reduced CPU load + RAM use)? If so, please provide benchmarks / profiles, as per our [optimization guidelines](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/optimization.html).\r\n\r\nI wouldn't say this is a performance optimization, but more like \"changing to what it used to be\" before #93831 in a non-breaking way. Mostly because I never understood why wasn't this done before.\r\n\r\n> W were also wondering if there could have been any reason for `get_file_as_bytes` to be used (caching perhaps?). Did you check if that may be the case?\r\n\r\nThe original code always used a direct `FileAccess` before #93831, with no statement of why `get_file_as_bytes` was used. The change from opening a `FileAccess` into using `get_file_as_bytes` was never questioned either. Probably due to how it matched `AudioStreamOggVorbis::load_from_file()`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3806946167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807317443","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3807317443","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3807317443,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i7w3D","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T20:12:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T20:12:50Z","body":"> I wouldn't say this is a performance optimization, but more like \"changing to what it used to be\" before https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/93831 in a non-breaking way. Mostly because I never understood why wasn't this done before.\r\n\r\nWhat's the motivation to change it if not for performance purposes? Every change comes with some risk, and we especially shouldn't be changing code because we don't understand what it does.\r\n\r\n> The original code always used a direct FileAccess before https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/93831, with no statement of why get_file_as_bytes was used. The change from opening a FileAccess into using get_file_as_bytes was never questioned either. Probably due to how it matched AudioStreamOggVorbis::load_from_file().\r\n\r\nThat's a good indication that switching back is probably safe, but not a guarantee. cc @cherrythecool","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807317443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807434823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3807434823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3807434823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i8NhH","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T20:41:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T20:55:59Z","body":"Compiled a build using `scons target=editor production=yes`.\r\n\r\nFor testing, I decided to import hundreds of WAV files(a total of 2.3GiB, the biggest WAV file having 88.7 MiB):\r\n\r\n| Build  | Import time | Maximum memory usage |\r\n|--------|-------------|--------------|\r\n| Before | 13s         | 4.1 GiB      |\r\n| After  | 24s         | 2.2 GiB      |\r\n\r\nIn the end, it trades memory usage for higher import times. Although if we enabled import options like downsampling to mono or decreasing the mix rate, memory usage would be much higher while import times would be closer to each other.\r\n\r\nI might do more benchmarks.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807434823/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807459332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3807459332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3807459332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7i8TgE","user":{"login":"cherrythecool","id":138817584,"node_id":"U_kgDOCEYwMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138817584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool","html_url":"https://github.com/cherrythecool","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cherrythecool/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T20:47:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T20:47:49Z","body":"> The original code always used a direct FileAccess before #93831, with no statement of why get_file_as_bytes was used. The change from opening a FileAccess into using get_file_as_bytes was never questioned either. Probably due to how it matched AudioStreamOggVorbis::load_from_file().\r\n\r\nsorry for not explaining back then, but *if i recall correctly*, i used `get_file_as_bytes` due to some weird issue i was having where `FileAccess` and `FileAccessMemory` didn't work the same in some aspect? like there was something in the code that would trigger an assertion or error or *something* when using `FileAccessMemory`, but removing it seemed to cause no issues and never happened with regular `FileAccess`? i don't remember exactly why but if that isn't a problem anymore then i imagine switching things to use the actual file for reduced memory usage in importing would be an overall improvement :+1:","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3807459332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3808468649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3808468649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3808468649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jAJ6p","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T01:36:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T02:44:44Z","body":"After a few more benchmarks, I realized reading from file is *significantly slower* due to `FileAccess` reading frame by frame instead of a memory buffer.\r\n\r\nIf reading directly from file is desired nonetheless I know two ways of speeding it up:\r\n1. Make a temporary buffer to copy large chunks of data into memory before encoding it to float. I know this is what [`dr_wav`](https://github.com/mackron/dr_libs/blob/master/dr_wav.h) does normally with 4096 bytes at once.\r\n2. Implementing `dr_wav` itself. Which is actually #96545 and would do way more than that.\r\n\r\nWith `dr_wav`, loading from file has about the same speed as loading from buffer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3808468649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812872274","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3812872274","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3812872274,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jQ9BS","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T17:53:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T18:14:54Z","body":"> 1. Make a temporary buffer to copy large chunks of data into memory before encoding it to float. I know this is what [`dr_wav`](https://github.com/mackron/dr_libs/blob/master/dr_wav.h?rgh-link-date=2026-01-28T01%3A36%3A00Z) does normally with 4096 bytes at once.\r\n\r\nI managed to get this one working.\r\n\r\nInstead of making it read frame by frame from a `FileAccess`, we copy a 4KiB chunk into a `FixedVector` each time, then convert from it.\r\n\r\nOn my tests, there is little difference in time between loading from buffer and from file. Actually, from file seems to be slightly faster.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3812872274/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813066527","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115235#issuecomment-3813066527","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115235","id":3813066527,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jRscf","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T18:27:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T17:38:55Z","body":"Redid the benchmarks after the change, this time checking only the time comparison between from buffer and from file:\r\n\r\n| Build  | Time from buffer | Time from file |\r\n|--------|-------------|--------------|\r\n| `master` | 14584 ms         | 14536 ms      |\r\n| PR  | 14656 ms         | 14388 ms      |\r\n\r\nSkipped memory checks as I don't believe there would be a difference between the previous benchmark. But basically, the difference in time is negligible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3813066527/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]